        "original_id": "bef65c89-a10a-5eaf-891b-8e4845f6124f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Maurice Level, Alice Hoffman\n- Roles: writer, novelist, young-adult writer, children's writer\n- Organizations: Théâtre du Grand-Guignol\n- Places: Paris, Pigalle\n- Works: Practical Magic\n- Topics: macabre short stories, fiction, drama, film adaptation\n\nFacts:\n- Maurice Level was born on August 29, 1875, and he was a French writer of fiction and drama.\n- Maurice Level specialized in macabre short stories that were printed regularly in Paris newspapers.\n- Some of Maurice Level's stories were staged by the Théâtre du Grand-Guignol, a repertory company in Paris's Pigalle district known for melodramatic productions emphasizing blood and gore.\n- Alice Hoffman was born on March 16, 1952, and she is an American novelist and a writer of young-adult and children's books.\n- Alice Hoffman is best known for her 1995 novel Practical Magic.\n- Practical Magic was adapted into a film of the same name in 1998.\n- Maurice Level died on April 15, 1926.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
